    "chunk_size_bytes": 1665,
    "chunk_text": "Ropewalk Galle makes debut on Asia\u2019s 50 Best Bars - Extended list ranked #93\n\nRopewalk Galle, the world\u2019s first arrack-speciality bar, has made its debut on Asia\u2019s 50 Best Bars - Extended list ranked #93, the global travel and hospitality platform from the team behind The World\u2019s 50 Best Bars.\n\nThe recognition marks another milestone for the bar just over two years since opening, making it the only bar in Galle and the third out of Sri Lanka to be featured on the prestigious platform.\n\nLocated within the 300-year-old Galle Fort Hotel in the UNESCO World Heritage-listed Galle Fort, Ropewalk has become synonymous with modern Sri Lankan mixology, celebrating arrack, the island\u2019s indigenous spirit through premium arrack tastings and an ingredient-led cocktail programme.\n\nHome to an arrack wall featuring more than 75 expressions of Sri Lanka\u2019s national spirit, the bar has also been recognised by Cond\u00e9 Nast Traveller India as one of the region\u2019s Top 20 Bars.\n\nRopewalk continues to push the boundaries of Sri Lankan mixology through an evolving cocktail programme and international collaborations. Signature serves include the Ropewalk, featuring 45-day spice-infused Old Cask Arrack, with sous-vide ginger and lemongrass syrup, Only Nabeel Likes This, a blend of Old Reserve Arrack, kithul treacle and masala tea and Gunpowder, combining Paradise White Arrack with chilli, cucumber, lemongrass and ginger ale.\n\nThe bar has also collaborated with internationally acclaimed venues including COA (Hong Kong), The Elephant Room (Singapore), BARC (Kathmandu) and AMPM (Kolkata), further positioning Sri Lankan arrack on the global cocktail stage."
  },
