    "chunk_text": "ACT reaffirms commitment to advancing Sri Lanka\u2019s container transport industry\n\nThe Association of Container Transporters (ACT), the apex representative body of Sri Lanka\u2019s container transport industry, successfully concluded its\u00a041st Annual General Meeting (AGM) and Fellowship on\u00a026\u00a0June\u00a02026\u00a0at the Lotus Tower, Colombo, reaffirming its commitment to strengthening the country\u2019s logistics and supply chain sector through closer industry collaboration and constructive engagement with policymakers.\n\nThe AGM was attended by Anura Karunatilleka, Minister of Ports, Aviation and Energy, who graced the occasion as the Chief Guest, while Ruwan Kodituwakku, Deputy Minister, attended as the Guest of Honour. The event also brought together senior government officials, industry leaders, corporate members, and representatives from the ports, shipping, logistics and supply chain sectors.\n\nAs Sri Lanka\u2019s pioneering association representing container transport operators, ACT has played a vital role in supporting the country\u2019s import and export trade for over four decades.\n\nFACETS Sri Lanka to be held at Cinnamon Life from 4th to 6th January 2027\n\nAmbeon Securities hosts exclusive investor forum on Sri Lanka\u2019s economic and market outlook\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
