    "chunk_size_bytes": 1689,
    "chunk_text": "Dreamron College of Art & Beauty celebrates 20 years in business\n\nChairman Dr. Priyanka Perera and Directress Nisha Perera handing over a scholarship\n\nDreamron College of Art & Beauty recently celebrated its 20th anniversary, marking two decades of empowering youth, transforming the beauty industry, and contributing to the nation\u2019s economic development.\n\nParallel to the celebration, 20 students representing all regions of the country were awarded full scholarships.\n\nFurthermore, Dreamron has announced a 25 percent discount on all courses throughout the month of July, providing aspiring students with an excellent opportunity to pursue professional education at a reduced cost.\n\nFounded in 2006 as a nonprofit institution, under the leadership and concept of Dr. Priyanka Perera and the Dreamron Group, the institution was established with the mission of elevating Sri Lanka\u2019s beauty and wellness industry through internationally recognized education and professional training.\n\nOver the past two decades, Dreamron College of Art & Beauty has successfully trained more than 20,000 students, producing highly skilled beauty professionals who now serve both local\n\nand international markets. Many graduates have also emerged as successful entrepreneurs, salon owners, and industry leaders.\n\nThe institution offers a wide range of professional programs, including Hair Artistry, Beauty Therapy, Nail Care Technology, and Bridal Styling, along with diploma courses, vocational training programs, and government-recognized NVQ Level 4 and Level 5 qualifications. These programs are conducted under the guidance and approval of relevant national vocational and educational authorities."
  },
