    "language": "en",
    "md5": "3b33535e91eb1d3b593938efe671d167",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1616,
    "chunk_text": "The event, which included key addresses by Ministry Secretary K.A. Vimalenthirarajah and SLAB Acting Director and CEO Chanditha Ediriweera, highlights the state\u2019s strategic focus on leveraging automated compliance frameworks to boost national economic competitiveness.\n\nAddressing the delegates, Houla commended Sri Lanka\u2019s long-standing dedication to regional compliance architectures, recalling that the institution had hosted the joint APLAC and PAC meetings in the exact same location 11 years prior.\n\n\u201cToday we return not only with fond memories of this milestone but with renewed confidence in Sri Lankans and your economy, recognising your continuous adaptations and achievements in the past as well as the responsibility for the future,\u201d Houla stated.\n\nHe further noted that the rapid advancements in artificial intelligence, digital product passports, sustainability reporting and carbon border adjustment mechanisms are fundamentally reshaping modern assessment paradigms, transitioning accreditation from a technical function into a \u201cstrategic national asset\u201d.\n\nThe high-level forums also focused on long-term national growth, detailing strategic collaborations to upgrade Sri Lanka\u2019s laboratory frameworks, food safety systems, public health protection and export reliability.\n\nThe evening concluded with a vote of thanks by SLAB Chairman Air Vice Marshal (Retired) Prasanna Ranasinghe. By aligning local conformity protocols with international benchmarks, Sri Lankan products and services stand to gain frictionless entry and heightened trust across highly competitive global markets. (NF)"
  },
