    "chunk_text": "\u2018India Calling\u2019 forum set to unlock bilateral trade and investment barriers\n\nIn a major push to redefine economic ties between Sri Lanka and India, the Lanka India Business Association (LIBA) has announced the highly anticipated corporate forum, \u2018India Calling\u2019. Scheduled for August 6th at the Taj Samudra, Colombo, from 9:00 AM to 6:00 PM, the full-day event is designed to bridge commercial gaps, unpack regulatory friction, and establish a framework for shared cross-border prosperity.\n\nLIBA is hosting the forum to actively catalyze deeper private sector integration, moving bilateral talks from policy theory into actionable investment corridors. The event arrives at a critical juncture as Sri Lanka actively recalibrates its macroeconomic framework and eyes stronger integration with the Indian market.\n\nThe forum boasts an extraordinary lineup of keynote speakers flying in from India to address critical facets of the economic relationship:\n\nMontek Singh Ahluwalia: The former Deputy Chairman of India\u2019s Planning Commission and a key architect of India\u2019s 1991 economic reforms, Ahluwalia will discuss India\u2019s massive economic transformation, and the specific structural lessons Sri Lanka can adopt to drive its own recovery.\n\nProfessor C. Raja Mohan: One of India\u2019s leading foreign policy strategists and academics, Professor Mohan will present on the geopolitical necessity of \u201cshared prosperity\u201d as a sustainable, long-term strategy for regional stability.\n\nDevdutt Pattanaik: The renowned mythologist, author, and corporate consultant will offer an unconventional perspective, breaking down the \u201cMonsoon Market Myth\u201d to explain how deep-rooted cultural narratives shape consumer behavior and market dynamics in South Asia.\n\nFirst Capital sees 70% chance Central Bank will hold rates on July 21\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
