    "chunk_size_bytes": 1834,
    "chunk_text": "LCB Finance opens Wellawattta premier branch\n\nLanka Credit and Business Finance PLC (LCB Finance), having celebrated the 10th anniversary recently, opened its 25th branch in Wellawatte, which is the third branch of the company in the Colombo district.\n\nThe branch was declared open at a strategic location facing the Galle Road, Wellawatta, by Plantations and Agricultural Industries Deputy Minister Pradeep Sundaralingam and Member of Parliament Mujbar Rahuman.\n\nThe opening ceremony was graced by distinguished invitees, consisting of reputed\u00a0 \u00a0entrepreneurs, potential customers, well-wishers, Chairman Dushmantha Thotawatte and the board of directors of the company.\n\nChief Executive Officer and Executive Director K.G. Leelananda addressing the gathering stated that the company intends to provide its financial products and services to commercial establishments, businessmen, salaried individuals and the residents in Wellawatta, contributing towards their business, social and communal upliftment.\n\nLeelananda\u00a0 stated that the company\u2019s deposit\u00a0 products, consisting of\u00a0 the \u2018Podiththa\u2019 and \u2018Sihina Ayojana\u2019 investment savings schemes, fixed deposits and lending products, consisting of\u00a0 \u00a0business loans, gold loans, lease finance, housing loans, educational loans\u00a0 and consumer loan facilities, are designed\u00a0 to meet the requirements of the prospective trading and businesses enterprises, small or medium enterprises and to cater to the financial services required by the co-operative societies, with specific reference to removal of barriers to financing women\u2019s empowerment-related projects.\n\nHe also stated that the company has planned to expand its business operations by enhancing the branch network to 30 outlets by the end of this year, which includes Jaffna as a chosen town to establish a branch."
