    "chunk_size_bytes": 1446,
    "chunk_text": "Namal alleges critics face intimidation, calls for probe into reported suicides\n\nSri Lanka Podujana Peramuna (SLPP) National Organiser and MP Namal Rajapaksa has alleged that individuals who speak out against the Government are being subjected to intimidation and pressure, claiming that some have been \u201cdriven to suicide.\u201d\n\nAddressing a divisional meeting in Dedigama, Kegalle, on Saturday (18), Rajapaksa claimed that people who make statements against the Government are threatened and pressured during questioning.\n\n\u201cIt seems to me that this is the period with the highest number of suicides. Some people who spoke against the Government have been driven to take their own lives. Others are allegedly told during questioning that they too could end up taking their own lives,\u201d he alleged.\n\nRajapaksa called for investigations into the reported incidents, accusing the Government of using intimidation and suppression against its critics.\n\nDuring his address, he also criticised the Government\u2019s economic policies, tax measures, its treatment of public servants and investors, and alleged that it had failed to deliver on promises made to the public.\n\nRegarding the \u2018Gamin Gamata\u2019 program by the party, he said it was a great opportunity to connect with the people.\n\n\u201cIt was a valuable opportunity to engage directly with the people, listen to their concerns and understand their aspirations,\u201d he noted via a post on \u2018X.\u2019"
