    "chunk_size_bytes": 1928,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka-USA Business Council to host breakfast forum on \u2018The IP Trade Corridor\u2019\n\nInitiative on Wednesday 22 July aimed at strengthening the US-Sri Lanka\u00a0 economic partnership\u00a0through intellectual property protection\n\nThe Sri Lanka-USA Business Council (SLUSABC) of the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce will host \u201cThe IP Trade Corridor - Strengthening US-Sri Lanka Economic Partnership through Intellectual Property Protection\u201d, a breakfast forum on 22 July 2026 at Hilton Colombo Residences from 8.30 a.m. onwards.\n\nThe United States is Sri Lanka\u2019s single largest export destination, and intellectual property (IP) has become an increasingly decisive factor in sustaining and deepening this trade and investment relationship. American brands entrust Sri Lankan manufacturers with proprietary designs; US technology companies license software across the country; and a growing number of Sri Lankan exporters, IT firms and creative businesses are building brands and innovations of their own that require protection in markets abroad. A credible, well-enforced IP regime is what converts trust into trade, investment and technology transfer.\n\nThe forum is the latest in the Council\u2019s ongoing program of initiatives to deepen bilateral commercial ties, undertaken in collaboration with the US Embassy in Colombo. The session has been deliberately designed for a wide cross-section of the business community, not only legal practitioners and large corporates, but SMEs, exporters, manufacturers, technology and creative businesses, and entrepreneurs. It will move beyond legal theory to the practical questions businesses actually confront: how to register and defend a brand; what recourse is available when counterfeits surface in the market or at the border; what US buyers and investors expect of IP compliance; and how stronger IP protection translates into greater orders, investment and market access for Sri Lanka."
