    "chunk_size_bytes": 1788,
    "chunk_text": "England captain Harry Brook won his third successive toss of the series and saw his openers produce a record-breaking start.\n\nDuckett and Bethell had endured difficult outings earlier in the series, but both were in complete control at Lord\u2019s as India's bowlers struggled to find their length.\n\nTheir partnership became England's highest opening stand at Lord\u2019s and their highest-ever opening partnership against India before Bethell was dismissed for 91.\n\nDuckett continued to dominate, reaching his century from 108 balls before eventually falling after completing a century partnership with Root.\n\nRoot then combined with Buttler to power England towards a huge total. Buttler smashed four fours and three sixes in his unbeaten 41 from 13 balls as England finished on 387-3.\n\nIf this was Rohit Sharma's final international appearance at Lord\u2019s, it was a memorable one.\n\nThe former India captain produced a brilliant 138, scoring his 34th ODI century and keeping India in contention deep into the chase.\n\nRohit reached his hundred from 84 balls and repeatedly attacked England's bowlers with his trademark pull shot.\n\nTogether with Gill, he helped India reach 253-1 in the 38th over, briefly putting India ahead of England's scoring rate at the same stage of their innings.\n\nBut Rohit's dismissal in the following over changed the match.\n\nKohli then made 74, including his first international half-century at Lord\u2019s, but England's bowlers kept taking wickets as India's required run rate climbed.\n\nSam Curran finished with four wickets as England closed out a 27-run victory and secured a 2-1 series win.\n\nEngland 387-3 (50 overs): Duckett 141 (135), Bethell 91 (93), Root 74* (48); Krishna 2-69\n\nIndia 360-7 (50 overs): Rohit 138 (110), Gill 77 (84), Kohli 74 (60); Curran 4-75"
