    "md5": "c9883062c92a23a631eeb7f284d99110",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1107,
    "chunk_text": "Cybercrime: Selective action won\u2019t help\n\nThe Government of India\u2019s recent notice to Meta regarding WhatsApp\u2019s upcoming \u201cUsername\u201d feature is a welcome step. The concern that allowing users to register with a fictitious user name could lead to increased online fraud, phishing, impersonation, and difficulties in cybercrime investigations is valid.\n\nThe exact same \u201canonymous username\u201d system already exists on Facebook which is also owned by Meta. On Facebook, anyone can create a Page or Profile with any name and message users without revealing a phone number or proper real ID\n\nToday,\u00a0 one paper reported: \u201cAI women\u00a0 SWINDLING SRI LANKANS HAVE INCREASED.\u201d\n\nIf our government\u2019s concern is genuinely about public safety and preventing cybercrime, then the rules must be applied uniformly across all platforms. Selective action against only WhatsApp will not solve the problem in India and will only create confusion.\n\nI\u00a0 urge the government to clarify its policy and bring in uniform regulations for all social media platforms regarding anonymous registrations to reduce cybercrimes."
  },
  {
