    "chunk_text": "The third is the land issue. The war is over, therefore all the lands occupied must be handed over to the owners. During the war, the occupation of land was justified logically because of war which we clearly understand. The war is over and the LTTE is no more. Currently there are lands addressed by the Archaeology Department, Mahaveli Authority and Forest Department in various other names. All those lands should be released to the people. Yes, Rajapakse won the lands, but AKD can people\u2019s hearts by returning them.\n\nThe government even assured the residents of the plantations that they will distribute uncultivated land, to the Malaiyaha community through their infamous Hatton Declaration. So, give that land to the people as promised. These people have sacrificed their lives for over 200 years. They have shed blood and tears. Today the regional plantation companies are more powerful than the times bygone. This is because the regional plantation bosses are alleged to be very close with the President. Therefore, they are randomly using the power vested in them against the poor\n\nQWhy can\u2019t you work on these requests while you are with the rest of the parties without separating yourselves?\n\nWe are very much a part of the opposition. We wanted to raise our issues so that it will be heard by the government in power. The Media did not reach us to hear our issues six months ago, but they have reached us now because we formed this platform. I don\u2019t find fault with the other opposition parties. Other parties in the opposition have their own list of priorities. We cannot force them to focus on our issues. They support our stance regarding constitution, provincial council elections and land.\n\nQDo you mean to say that there is no conflict within the opposition?"
