    "chunk_size_bytes": 1571,
    "chunk_text": "Police stations under watch over drug raids; STF to step in where police fail\n\nColombo, July 21 (Daily Mirror) - Public Security Minister Ananda Wijepala said that if a local police station fails to take action against drug-related activities in its area, he is prepared to deploy other police divisions or the Police Special Task Force (STF) to conduct raids.\n\nThe Minister said a zero-tolerance policy has been adopted towards failures in acting on narcotics-related information and said that police officers and the STF have been instructed not to ignore any complaints or intelligence regarding illegal drug activities.\n\nThe remarks come amid reports that more than 1,000 police officers have been removed from service over various offences. The Minister had earlier said that some officers were dismissed for alleged involvement in drug trafficking and maintaining links with organised criminal groups.\n\nHe also said several officers had been removed for offences including neglect of duty and accepting bribes.\n\nSpeaking on the government\u2019s drug prevention strategy at an event in Kurunegala on Sunday, Wijepala said authorities would adopt a different approach towards drug users and traffickers. He said that simply arresting and imprisoning drug users would not provide a lasting solution, and that users should instead be treated as individuals requiring medical assistance and directed towards rehabilitation programmes.\n\nHowever, he said strict legal action would be taken against drug traffickers and distributors who contribute to the spread of narcotics."
