    "chunk_size_bytes": 584,
    "chunk_text": "Rs 26.2 million spent for Rohana Wijeweera\u2019s family\n\nColombo, July 21 (Daily Mirror) - Public funds of Rs. 26,278,052 has been spent for the late founder of the Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna (JVP) Rohana Wijeweera's family since his demise, it has been revealed.\n\nThe answer given by the government to a question raised by Opposition MP Ajith P. Perera has revealed that the Sri Lankan government has originally spent the said amount to support Chithrangani Wijeweera and six children.\n\nHowever the government currently supports Ms. Wijeweera and her eldest daughter with special needs."
