    "chunk_size_bytes": 1096,
    "chunk_text": "Harsha lauds Southern Expressway emergency roadside assistance\n\nColombo, July 21 (Daily Mirror) - Samagi Jana Balawegaya (SJB) MP Harsha de Silva has praised the Southern Expressway's emergency roadside assistance service after he and his wife experienced a tyre-related incident while travelling on the expressway.\n\nIn a post on X, the MP said the incident occurred on the Southern Expressway last evening and described it as \"a bit of a scary situation.\"\n\nDe Silva said that after calling the expressway's '1969 Emergency Roadside Assistance' service, a response team arrived within minutes and helped resolve the issue.\n\n\"They were professional and courteous. In fact, they wouldn't let me change; did it themselves, which I don't think is even their responsibility,\" he said.\n\nThe MP also urged motorists to regularly inspect their vehicles, particularly their tyres.\n\n\"Everyone: check your tyres. Lucky for us I was at only 100 km/h and it was the rear,\" he wrote, thanking the Road Development Authority (RDA) and the Southern Expressway emergency response team for their prompt assistance."
  },
