    "chunk_text": "US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Washington remained open to negotiations with Iran, but that \"it has to be real\". It remains unclear whether Tehran will offer anything that President Donald Trump would consider \"real\".\n\nA barrage of US strikes has not forced Tehran to loosen its grip on the strait, through which about one-fifth of the world's crude oil and natural gas had been shipped before the war. The US carried out more airstrikes early on Tuesday, while Iran attacked a tanker in the waterway, forcing its crew to abandon the vessel.\n\nThe US military's Central Command said it had targeted \"Iranian military command centres, maritime capabilities, missile and drone launch sites and air defence systems\". It also released more footage showing bombings at sites in Iran.\n\n\"American forces remain postured and prepared to hold Iran accountable for unwarranted aggression toward civilian mariners seeking to freely and openly transit the strait,\" the command said.\n\nIranian state media reported explosions in Fars, Hormozgan, Ilam, Kerman, and Sistan and Baluchistan provinces. The British military's United Kingdom Maritime Trade Operations centre said a tanker was attacked early on Tuesday in the strait off Oman, forcing the crew to leave the ship.\n\nIran's paramilitary Revolutionary Guard claimed responsibility for that attack as well as two other attacks on ships on Monday in the waterway. The route around Oman had been the one the US military encouraged ships to use to avoid Iran's control.\n\nTehran also continued strikes on US-allied countries across the Middle East. Jordan's military said Iran targeted it with five drones and three missiles on Tuesday, all of which were intercepted."
