    "chunk_text": "CA Sri Lanka also called for broad reforms to tax administration, including risk-based audit systems, stronger digitalisation, more consistent interpretation of tax laws and the establishment of an independent Tax Ombudsman to provide investors with an impartial mechanism for resolving administrative disputes.\n\nThe institute also recommended modernising Sri Lanka\u2019s Advance Pricing Agreement programme by expanding its scope, simplifying compliance requirements and aligning procedures with international standards to provide multinational companies with greater tax certainty.\n\n\u201cForeign Direct Investment remains one of the most important drivers of economic growth, employment generation, technology transfer and long-term national prosperity,\u201d CA Sri Lanka said, adding that the reforms are intended to strengthen investor confidence and improve Sri Lanka\u2019s competitiveness in an increasingly complex global investment environment."
