    "chunk_size_bytes": 1120,
    "chunk_text": "Imagine if even a small proportion of what is currently allocated to signage, branding and hospitality was redirected towards collaborative experience design, immersive environments, creative storytelling and meaningful activations.\n\nThe commercial return would almost certainly be greater than another oversized logo on a stage backdrop.\n\nThat requires every marketing team in Sri Lanka to ask a different question. Not, \"Which event should we sponsor?\" But rather, \"What experience could only our brand create?\" Because that is where genuine differentiation lies.\n\nSri Lanka has never lacked creativity. What it has often lacked is the confidence to think bigger about the role brands can play in culture.\n\nThe next generation of successful marketing campaigns will not be built around the biggest media buy or the most prominent logo. They will be built around experiences that people actively choose to be part of.\n\nAs marketers, we have spent decades asking how we can get consumers to notice our brands. Perhaps it is time we asked a far more important question. How can we create something they will never forget?"
