    "md5": "d047a64a1a87f55f52a14ac3c855b238",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1727,
    "chunk_text": "SLWJA condemns Parliament Select Committee over summoning journalists\n\nThe Sri Lanka Working Journalists\u2019 Association (SLWJA) yesterday condemned the decision to summon two BBC Sinhala Service journalists before the Parliamentary Privileges Committee, describing the move as media repression and a threat to freedom of expression.\n\nIn a statement, the association said BBC producer Ishara Dhanasekara and journalist Sampath Dissanayake had been directed to appear before the committee at 2 p.m. on 23 July following a complaint by MP Lakmali Hemachandra and under instructions from the Speaker.\n\n\u201cThis marks yet another dark stain in Sri Lanka\u2019s history of media repression,\u201d the statement said.\n\nThe summons relates to BBC Sinhala\u2019s coverage of a meeting of the Women Parliamentarians\u2019 Caucus, which questioned National Child Protection Authority (NCPA) officials over delays in police investigations into allegations of child abuse involving the Atamasthanadhipathi of Anuradhapura Ven. Pallegama Hemarathana Thera.\n\nThe SLWJA argued that the Caucus is an informal body without legal authority and that summoning journalists for reporting on its proceedings posed \u201ca serious threat to freedom of speech and media independence.\u201d\n\nThe association alleged that the Government was seeking to conceal failures and irregularities by curtailing press freedom and intimidating journalists through the misuse of parliamentary privileges.\n\nThe SLWJA called on the Government and parliamentary authorities to immediately withdraw the summons and urged media organisations, civil society groups and the public to oppose what it described as a repressive approach that undermines democracy, transparency and media freedom."
  },
