    "chunk_size_bytes": 1587,
    "chunk_text": "Gunmen open fire at Devinuwara house\n\nColombo, July 22 (Daily Mirror) - A group of unidentified individuals who arrived in a car opened fire at a house behind the Devinuwara Sri Vishnu Devalaya before fleeing the scene, police said.\n\nNo injuries or damage to the house or other property were reported. However, several bullets fired from a 9mm firearm struck the front wall of the residence.\n\nPolice suspect the shooting may be linked to a dispute between two organized crime groups, reportedly stemming from a conflict involving Kavadi dance troupes scheduled to participate in an upcoming procession at the Devinuwara Devalaya.\n\nFollowing the incident, an audio recording allegedly released by an organized crime figure and suspected drug trafficker known as \"Dehibale Malli\" has been circulating on social media.\n\nThe shooting comes amid heightened tensions after another video containing an alleged audio threat by organized crime figure and suspected drug trafficker Mohamed Najeem Mohamed Imran, alias Kanjipani Imran, targeting the Basnayake Nilame of the Kataragama Devalaya, also surfaced online.\n\nThilina Madushanka, Basnayake Nilame of the Devinuwara Sri Vishnu Devalaya, said he would lodge a formal complaint with the police over the threats.\n\nInvestigators also revealed that a suspect currently in prison had previously made phone calls demanding money from the Basnayake Nilame. The matter had already been under investigation by the Walana Anti-Vice Unit.\n\nPolice have launched further investigations into the shooting and the alleged criminal links behind the incident."
  },
