    "chunk_text": "PM reviews progress of education digitalisation programme\n\nColombo, July 22 (Daily Mirror) - Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya has reviewed the progress of Sri Lanka\u2019s education digitalisation programme and future initiatives aimed at strengthening digital facilities in schools.\n\nThe Prime Minister held a discussion at Parliament on July 21 with officials from the Prime Minister\u2019s Office, Ministry of Education, Ministry of Digital Economy, GovTech, Sri Lanka Air Force, Sri Lanka Telecom, Dialog and other institutions to assess the ongoing digitalisation efforts.\n\nThe discussion focused on providing the required digital infrastructure to support the new education reforms introduced by the government. Under the guidance of Prime Minister\u2019s Secretary Pradeep Saputhanthree and a specially appointed task force, several projects have been implemented over the past year, including the installation of digital infrastructure in schools, provision of smart boards, internet facilities and computers.\n\nOfficials informed the meeting that the Human Resource Management (HRM) module of the National Education Management Information System (NEMIS), developed with technical assistance from the Sri Lanka Air Force, has been fully completed in four provinces. The remaining five provinces are expected to be included within the next three months.\n\nThe NEMIS system will be used for teacher transfers in the future, and the process has already commenced in the Sabaragamuwa and Western provinces. The Human Resource Management module will also be updated continuously with new data.\n\nThe progress of providing internet facilities to schools through fibre technology was also reviewed. It was decided to complete the fibre connectivity programme by December 31, while wireless or satellite technology will be considered for schools where fibre connections are not practically feasible."
