    "chunk_text": "The progress of providing internet facilities to schools through fibre technology was also reviewed. It was decided to complete the fibre connectivity programme by December 31, while wireless or satellite technology will be considered for schools where fibre connections are not practically feasible.\n\nThe meeting also discussed future plans, including the full implementation of the Learning Management System (LMS) and NEMIS platforms, connecting all schools to these systems, upgrading the e-Thaksalawa online learning platform, and signing an agreement between the Ministry of Education and GovTech for further digital transformation of the education sector.\n\nMinister of Children and Women\u2019s Affairs Saroja Savitri Paulraj, Deputy Minister of Digital Economic Affairs Eranga Weeraratne, Deputy Minister of Education Dr. Madhura Seneviratne, Deputy Minister of Mass Media Dr. Kaushalya Ariyaratne, government officials and senior ministry officials also participated in the discussion."
