    "chunk_text": "AmCham Sri Lanka and Standard Chartered to bring int\u2019l cybersecurity expertise with \u2018SeCure 2026\u2019\n\nCyber security expert Chris Fleming to head exclusive executive session\n\nThe American Chamber of Commerce in Sri Lanka (AmCham Sri Lanka), in partnership with Standard Chartered Sri Lanka, will host \u201cSeCure 2026: Strengthening Organizations Against Tomorrow\u2019s Threats\u201d on 4 August, at the Courtyard by Marriott, Colombo.\n\nThis executive breakfast forum will bring together senior business leaders, cybersecurity professionals, policymakers and technology experts for a timely discussion on one of the greatest risks facing organizations today- the rapidly evolving cyber threat landscape.\n\nCyber and digital fraud risks are no longer confined to technology teams. Ransomware, payment fraud, supply chain compromise and third-party vulnerabilities can disrupt operations, damage customer trust and create significant financial and regulatory exposure. For business leaders, the priority is no longer simply preventing incidents, but building the governance, response capability and decision-making discipline needed to keep organizations resilient.\n\nRecognizing the importance of equipping Sri Lankan businesses with insights drawn from international best practice, AmCham Sri Lanka has partnered with Standard Chartered Sri Lanka to bring Chris Fleming, Executive Director and Head of Client & Third-Party Security at Standard Chartered, to Colombo for an exclusive\n\nWith extensive experience leading cybersecurity and third-party security programs across one of the world\u2019s leading international banks, Fleming brings a global perspective on cyber resilience, governance and risk management. His work spans enterprise security strategy, threat intelligence, third-party risk and cyber governance, giving him practical insight into how organizations can better anticipate, prepare for, and respond to today\u2019s increasingly sophisticated cyber threats."
  },
