    "language": "en",
    "md5": "9a4e396f6cb98d24d6b94abee97ca555",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1899,
    "chunk_text": "Singer Sri Lanka joins Dialog Pay ecosystem\n\nFrom left: Dialog Axiata Group Chief Marketing Officer Lasantha Theverapperuma, Dialog Enterprise Group Chief Officer Navin Pieris, Singer Sri Lanka Director Marketing Janmesh Antony and Singer Sri Lanka CEO Mahesh Wijewardene\n\nDialog Axiata PLC announced its partnership with Singer Sri Lanka PLC, enabling the customers to make secure and convenient digital payments using Dialog Pay across over 420 Singer showrooms islandwide.\n\nAs one of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading retailers of consumer durables, Singer offers a wide portfolio including consumer electronics, home appliances, furniture, digital products, kitchen appliances and agricultural machinery.\n\nWith Dialog Pay integrated at Singer billing counters, the customers can simply scan the LankaQR code using the Dialog Pay app or MyDialog app to complete transactions, ensuring a fast, secure and seamless checkout experience across one of the country\u2019s largest retail networks, supported by Singer\u2019s trusted legacy of over 145 years, serving millions of customers annually.\n\nCommenting on the partnership, Singer Group Group Managing Director Mahesh Wijewardene said, \u201cAt Singer, customer convenience and innovation remain at the heart of everything we do. Our partnership with Dialog Pay reflects our commitment to providing the customers with secure, seamless and rewarding payment experiences across our nationwide retail network. As digital adoption continues to grow, we are pleased to collaborate with Dialog in making everyday shopping easier while supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s digital transformation.\u201d\n\nDialog Pay, available through the Dialog Pay app and MyDialog app, brings together connectivity, digital payments and financial services within a single ecosystem, supporting Dialog\u2019s vision of making digital payments simpler, more accessible and more rewarding for every Sri Lankan."
  },
