    "description": "SLCGE invites SME apparel manufacturers to join unified industry platform",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-news/SLCGE-invites-SME-apparel-manufacturers-to-join-unified-industry-platform/273-346369",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1784747185.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-07-23-dailymirrorlk-033f933e-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "428d5dacfb38242bf42c01ee3caeac0b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1959,
    "chunk_text": "SLCGE invites SME apparel manufacturers to join unified industry platform\n\nThe Sri Lanka Chamber of Garment Exporters (SLCGE), established in 1994, has invited the small and medium-sized apparel manufacturers from across Sri Lanka to join the chamber and become part of a unified platform committed to strengthening the country\u2019s apparel sector.\n\nHaving represented and supported Sri Lanka\u2019s apparel industry for more than three decades, the SLCGE said its renewed membership drive aims to bring together established exporters and aspiring exporters under one collective industry voice, at a time when the global apparel markets are becoming increasingly competitive.\n\nThe chamber noted that greater collaboration among the small and medium enterprises (SME) apparel manufacturers is essential to building a stronger, more resilient and export-oriented industry. By working together, the manufacturers can share knowledge, address common challenges and collectively explore new opportunities in international markets.\n\nThrough the SLCGE membership, the apparel manufacturers will have the opportunity to collaborate with fellow industry participants, explore new and untapped international business opportunities and support collective initiatives aimed at improving direct market access.\n\nThe members will also be able to gain industry knowledge, market intelligence and exposure to best practices through workshops, seminars, networking events and capacity-building programmes conducted or facilitated by the chamber.\n\n\u201cThe SME apparel manufacturers are an important part of Sri Lanka\u2019s export economy but many continue to face challenges in accessing markets, finance, technology and timely policy information. By joining the SLCGE, the manufacturers can become part of a stronger collective platform that enables them to share knowledge, build industry connections and pursue new business opportunities,\u201d said SLCGE President Nishantha Bakmeege."
  },
