    "md5": "6236efb228dc6d2f4fc67190a82278f4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1657,
    "chunk_text": "Blue Economy: Unlocking Sri Lanka\u2019s Ocean Potential Through Sustainable Development\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s identity has always been inseparable from the ocean. Surrounded by the Indian Ocean and strategically positioned along one of the world\u2019s busiest east-west maritime trade routes, the island possesses an extraordinary natural advantage. For centuries, the sea has supported trade, fisheries, tourism, and cultural heritage. Today, however, the ocean represents something even more significant\u2014a powerful engine for sustainable economic growth through the development of the Blue Economy.\n\nThe Blue Economy refers to the sustainable use of ocean resources to generate economic growth, improve livelihoods, and create jobs while preserving the health of marine ecosystems. Unlike traditional economic models that often exploit natural resources without considering long-term consequences, the Blue Economy balances economic development with environmental protection and social responsibility. As Environmental, Social and Governance (ESG) principles become increasingly important to businesses and investors, Sri Lanka has an opportunity to position itself as a regional leader in sustainable ocean-based development.\n\nWith an Exclusive Economic Zone (EEZ) that is several times larger than its land area, Sri Lanka possesses vast untapped marine resources. These include fisheries, shipping, ports, renewable energy, marine biotechnology, aquaculture, coastal tourism, and ocean-based research. Harnessing these opportunities responsibly could contribute significantly to economic recovery, export earnings, employment generation, and climate resilience."
  },
