    "language": "en",
    "md5": "c65de912401b04a3afec03786e18389e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1915,
    "chunk_text": "Circular Economy: Turning Waste into Value Through Sustainable Innovation\n\nFor decades, economic development has largely followed a linear model of \u201ctake, make, and dispose.\u201d Raw materials are extracted, transformed into products, consumed, and eventually discarded as waste. While this approach has supported industrial growth and improved living standards, it has also placed unprecedented pressure on natural resources, ecosystems, and the global climate. As populations grow and consumption continues to rise, the limitations of this traditional economic model have become increasingly evident.\n\nThe concept of the circular economy offers a compelling alternative. Rather than viewing waste as an inevitable by-product of economic activity, a circular economy seeks to eliminate waste by designing products, systems, and business models that keep materials in use for as long as possible. It focuses on reducing resource consumption, extending product life cycles, recovering valuable materials, and regenerating natural systems.\n\nFor Sri Lanka, embracing circular economy principles presents an opportunity to improve resource efficiency, reduce environmental pollution, create new industries, generate employment, and strengthen long-term economic resilience. As sustainability becomes a key driver of business competitiveness, circular innovation is emerging as a cornerstone of responsible economic development.\n\nRegenerate natural systems by reducing environmental impact and restoring ecosystems.\n\nUnlike the traditional linear model, the circular economy encourages businesses to design products that are durable, repairable, reusable, and recyclable. Materials are continuously circulated within the economy instead of being discarded after a single use.\n\nThis approach transforms waste into a valuable resource while reducing the need for virgin raw materials and lowering greenhouse gas emissions."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
