    "md5": "921a27f7e2d6eae57768de7e8eb0310e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2010,
    "chunk_text": "Leading growth through literacy: How Seylan \u2018Pahasara\u2019 is building Sri Lanka\u2019s future through grassroots education\n\nThe Seylan \u2018Pahasara\u2019 Library Project has grown into one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most enduring corporate education initiatives, reflecting Seylan Bank\u2019s long-term commitment to creating equitable access to learning while nurturing financially literate, socially-responsible future citizens. Launched in 2013 to commemorate the Bank\u2019s 25th anniversary, the programme has evolved into a flagship Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) initiative, strengthening library infrastructure in schools across the island while expanding educational opportunities through technology, financial literacy, and community engagement.\n\nAt a time when equitable access to quality education continues to shape social mobility and national development, Seylan \u2018Pahasara\u2019 demonstrates how meaningful private sector partnerships can complement Sri Lanka\u2019s education system by creating opportunities that extend well beyond the classroom. By investing in libraries as centres of learning, creativity, and community engagement, the programme is helping cultivate the necessary knowledge, values, and life skills that empower future generations.\n\nAs the programme approaches the landmark of its 300th library, Assistant General Manager \u2013 Marketing & Sales, Asiri Abhayaratne, reflects on the journey and the vision that continues to shape Seylan \u2018Pahasara\u2019.\n\nQ: As Seylan \u2018Pahasara\u2019 approaches its 300th library, what does this milestone represent for the Bank?\n\nA: Reaching the 300-library milestone represents far more than a numerical achievement. It reflects over a decade of consistent investment in Sri Lanka\u2019s future through education. Since opening the very first \u2018Pahasara\u2019 library on 1 March 2013, our objective has remained unchanged, to empower children by improving access to quality learning environments and creating opportunities that extend well beyond the classroom."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
