    "md5": "f7b625a69f5024d2c9b5f85446b5eb16",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1668,
    "chunk_text": "Libraries became the ideal platform because they are gateways to opportunity, imagination, and lifelong learning, not simply places that house books. They are spaces where curiosity is nurtured, confidence grows, and young minds begin to discover their potential. We wanted to combine the habit of reading with the habit of saving and creating a meaningful connection between knowledge and responsibility.\n\nA: While our core purpose has remained unchanged, the programme itself has grown significantly. Initially, our focus was on establishing or refurbishing school libraries and providing quality books. Today, each \u2018Pahasara\u2019 library is supported by a much broader ecosystem of learning that combines physical infrastructure with experiential education and digital learning opportunities.\n\nOne of the most valuable additions has been \u2018Pahasara Week\u2019, which has become an integral component of every library opening. Rather than limiting our contribution to infrastructure, we dedicate an entire week to engaging students through activities that support their academic, personal, and social development.\n\nThese activities even further the development of soft skills through the inclusion of financial literacy programmes, mathematics camps, arts, sports, leadership development, culinary experiences, and other interactive learning opportunities. Students are introduced to practical financial concepts from an early age while also developing creativity, teamwork, communication, and problem-solving skills. The objective is to expose children to experiences that many schools may have limited access to while encouraging confidence and holistic development."
  },
