    "chunk_text": "Continuing its leadership, LB Finance became the first financial institution in Sri Lanka to quantify and independently verify avoided greenhouse gas emissions, commonly known as Carbon Handprint. Unlike traditional carbon footprint reporting, Carbon Handprint captures the positive environmental impact created through financing activities that enable customers to reduce their own emissions. During the 2025/26 financial year, the Company\u2019s vehicle and solar financing portfolio generated 4,018 tonnes of independently verified avoided carbon dioxide emissions, highlighting the powerful role responsible finance can play in accelerating Sri Lanka\u2019s transition to a low-carbon economy.\n\nRecognising that sustainable finance extends well beyond climate action alone, LB Finance has established a comprehensive Environmental and Social Management System (ESMS). By integrating environmental and social risk assessments into lending decisions, the Company encourages customers to adopt more sustainable business practices while strengthening responsible financing across its portfolio.\n\nThese efforts are complemented by a strong focus on operational sustainability. Expanded solar power generation across the branch network, improved resource efficiency, lower operational emissions and paperless banking through the LB CIM digital platform enable customers to access convenient financial services with a reduced environmental footprint."
