    "chunk_size_bytes": 905,
    "chunk_text": "The maritime industry is now entering a period in which customers, investors and regulators are placing increasing emphasis on ESG performance. Cleaner supply chains, lower emissions and responsible governance are becoming competitive advantages rather than compliance requirements.\n\nThis presents both a challenge and an opportunity for ports.\n\nUltimately, the ports that lead the next generation of global trade may not simply be those that move the most cargo. They are likely to be the ports that move cargo most responsibly.\n\nThrough initiatives ranging from equipment electrification and digitalisation to biodiversity conservation and community partnerships, CICT demonstrates that the future of port sustainability is not built around a collection of individual projects. It is built around a different way of operating.\n\nThat may prove to be the industry\u2019s most important transformation of all."
