    "md5": "a7bde4a7ab3e8b93f8fbe25d0d262e83",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1691,
    "chunk_text": "Governance underpins the Group\u2019s approach to ethics, compliance and risk management. Effective oversight, transparent decision-making and responsible conduct enable Advantis to manage risk, maintain stakeholder confidence and build resilience across its operations and relationships.\n\nRestoring Ecosystems Through Advantis Blue C and Advantis Green C\n\nAlongside action within its operations, Advantis is contributing to ecosystem recovery through Advantis Blue C and Advantis Green C. These programmes combine corporate resources, scientific expertise and employee participation to support the restoration of coastal and terrestrial environments.\n\nAdvantis Blue C supports the conservation and restoration of blue carbon ecosystems while contributing towards enhancing Sri Lanka\u2019s blue carbon sequestration capacity. Its flagship intervention is the Accelerated Natural Regeneration of Mangroves project at the Anawilundawa Ramsar Wetland.\n\nThe programme also includes an 8.9-hectare mangrove restoration site at Pubudugama, where the second phase commenced in 2024. Research visits support data collection, while employee participation provides direct exposure to the ecological value of mangrove ecosystems.\n\nBuilding on this experience, Advantis introduced Advantis Green C to focus on terrestrial ecosystem restoration. The programme covers 15.26 hectares at the Frocester Estate in Govinna and aims to establish a resilient and self-sustaining natural landscape.\n\nThe initiative includes the reintroduction of native plant species, improvement of soil health, increased water infiltration and retention, enhanced biodiversity and the creation of stable habitats for flora and fauna."
