    "chunk_size_bytes": 1455,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cStaying the Course\u201d SAGT shaping the course for a Sustainable Future\n\nSouth Asia Gateway Terminals (SAGT) is Sri Lanka\u2019s first Public Private Partnership (PPP) container terminal. Since commencing operations in 1999, SAGT has played a transformative role in the Port of Colombo and consistently supported the Port\u2019s aspiration of serving as South Asia\u2019s preeminent gateway hub for global trade.\n\nSAGT has set industry benchmarks in operational excellence and has been instrumental in elevating the Port of Colombo\u2019s global standing throughout the years. The terminal has repeatedly demonstrated its ability to outperform its original design capacity of 1.1 million TEUs, achieving annual throughput volumes exceeding 2 million TEUs in 2018, 2019, and 2024 through sustained productivity improvements.\n\n\u201cOur commitment to sustainability is woven into every aspect of our operations,\u201d said Ted Muttiah, CCO of SAGT. \u201cBy embedding ESG principles into our core strategy, we ensure operational excellence while creating sustainable value for all our stakeholders\u201d\n\nSAGT stands as a cornerstone of the Port of Colombo, consistently proving that operational excellence and responsible practices are inseparable. As the only terminal in the Port of Colombo to consistently publish an independently accredited sustainability report aligned with global standards, SAGT has reinforced its commitment to transparency and long-term value creation."
  },
