    "chunk_text": "Driving a significant social milestone, SAGT has increased female representation from 4% to 6.9% over the past two reporting periods by integrating women into operational shift roles, with a target of 10% by 2029. To sustain this momentum, the Company promotes an equal environment by expanding career opportunities for females, implementing industry-first anti-sexual harassment and paternity leave policies, and establishing mentorship programs that empower the next generation of women in the maritime sector.\n\nDecarbonising operations remains a key priority for SAGT. The terminal has achieved a 21% reduction in GHG emissions intensity relative to its 2019/20 baseline by prioritising fleet modernisation and a comprehensive energy transition. A primary contributor to this decarbonisation has been the hybridisation of 28 of 31 RTG cranes, which now utilise approximately 58% less diesel per move compared to traditional units. Complementing this, a 460 kW rooftop solar PV system is fully operational, generating 44,000 kWh per month to meet 5% of total electricity needs, thereby directly reducing Scope 2 emissions\n\nWorkplace safety is prioritised through advanced technology, including fatigue- monitoring systems in yard cabs and enhanced halo lighting on mobile equipment, to reduce man-machine risks. Furthermore, ongoing investments in terminal gate automation, OCR, and the Vehicle Booking System improve truck turnaround times and logistics efficiency, directly contributing to lower Scope 3 emissions.\n\n\u201cOur commitment to sustainability is woven into every aspect of our operations,\u201d said Ted Muttiah, CCO of SAGT. \u201cBy embedding ESG principles into our core strategy, we ensure operational excellence while creating sustainable value for all our stakeholders.\u201d"
