    "chunk_size_bytes": 1635,
    "chunk_text": "JICA delegation visits EDB to strengthen future collaboration\n\nA delegation from the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) paid an official courtesy visit to the Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB), marking an important engagement between the two institutions to review their longstanding partnership and discuss future initiatives aimed at strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s export development and economic growth.\n\nThe visit introduced the newly appointed JICA Chief Representative of the JICA Sri Lanka Office, Shigeo Honzu, while also acknowledging the contribution of the outgoing JICA Chief Representative, Kenji Kuronuma, who played a significant role in advancing cooperation between JICA and Sri Lanka during his tenure.\n\nDuring the meeting, the JICA delegation held discussions with the Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of the Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB), Mangala Wijesinghe along with Erandika Dissanayake, Acting Director General of EDB and other EDB officials.\n\nThe discussions focused on the successful collaboration between EDB and JICA over the past years, highlighting the impact of joint programmes, capacity-building initiatives, technical cooperation and support extended towards enhancing Sri Lanka\u2019s export competitiveness.\n\nEDB officials expressed their appreciation for JICA\u2019s continued partnership and contribution towards strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s export and investment ecosystem. The meeting also explored future areas of cooperation, including new initiatives to support exporters, improve market access, enhance institutional capabilities and promote sustainable export growth."
