    "chunk_text": "The High Commission added that pilgrimage visa requests should continue to be forwarded through the Ministry of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs, and applications can be submitted as groups of 10 or more.\n\nThe High Commission also said a special expedited process has been introduced for senior citizens visiting ICAC for biometric procedures to minimise waiting times.\n\n\u201cCapturing biometrics will ensure that their passage through Indian Immigration on arrival in India is smooth and convenient,\u201d it said.\n\nClarifying further, the High Commission said there is no visa fee applicable for Sri Lankan pilgrims whose applications are submitted through the prescribed procedure.\n\nHowever, applicants are required to pay a visa service fee of Rs. 1,855 to the Indian Consular Application Centres for processing services."
