    "md5": "fe383bb6200324fe0324b72c093abf36",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1757,
    "chunk_text": "BASL rejects government MP\u2019s claims, challenges MP to repeat allegations outside Parliament\n\nColombo, July 24 (Daily Mirror) - The Bar Association of Sri Lanka (BASL) today strongly rejected allegations made in Parliament by Government MP Asitha Niroshana Egoda Withanage against BASL President Rajeev Amarasuriya, describing the claims as \u201cutterly false, baseless, and made with malicious intent.\u201d\n\nNational People\u2019s Power (NPP) MP Asitha Niroshana Egoda Withanage, speaking in Parliament today, claimed that BASL President Rajeev Amarasuriya had held discussions with Opposition Leader Sajith Premadasa, who had allegedly promised him the Western Province Chief Ministerial candidacy at the upcoming Provincial Council election in exchange for his support.\n\nThe BASL challenged MP Asitha Niroshana Egoda Withanage to repeat the allegations outside Parliament without the protection of parliamentary privilege, stating that doing so would enable the appropriate legal consequences to follow.\n\nIssuing a statement, the BASL expressed \u201cdeep dismay\u201d over what it described as false utterances made under parliamentary privilege and accused the MP of attempting to mislead the public through unfounded and defamatory allegations.\n\nThe BASL further expressed concern over what it termed the abuse of parliamentary privilege, stating that such remarks sought to misguide the public and undermine confidence in the legal profession. It also maintained that \u201ccheap political attacks\u201d on the BASL would not succeed, adding that Sri Lanka\u2019s legal fraternity remains united in defending its independence and integrity.\n\nThe BASL statement was signed by its Deputy President, President\u2019s Counsel Rienzie Arsecularatne, and Secretary Nalin De Silva."
