    "md5": "b719040a4f626afec388004f75ad55e4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1858,
    "chunk_text": "China pledges deeper defence ties with Sri Lanka as Beijing marks PLA anniversary\n\nFrom left: Chinese Ambassador Qi Zhenhong, Defence Deputy Minister Major General (Retd.) Aruna Jayasekara and Chinese Embassy Defence Attach\u00e9 Senior Colonel Fu Xiao\n\nChina used celebrations marking the 99th anniversary of the People\u2019s Liberation Army (PLA) to reaffirm its strategic partnership with Sri Lanka, with senior Chinese officials pledging deeper defence cooperation while presenting Beijing\u2019s military modernisation as a contributor to regional stability and global peace.\n\nAddressing a reception hosted by the Chinese Embassy in Colombo Attended by Defence Deputy Minister Major General (Retd.) Aruna Jayasekara, Chinese Ambassador Qi Zhenhong said military relations between the two countries had continued to deepen through defence consultations, personnel training, equipment cooperation and technical exchanges, while reiterating Beijing\u2019s commitment to strengthening strategic trust with Sri Lanka.\n\n\u201cThe military-to-military relations between China and Sri Lanka are battle-tested,\u201d Ambassador Qi said.\n\nHe noted that China had provided emergency supplies worth RMB 10 million to Sri Lanka\u2019s\u00a0 Defence Ministry following Cyclone Ditwah, describing it as part of Beijing\u2019s continuing support for the country.\n\n\u201cAs always, China stands ready to work with Sri Lanka to build strategic trust and continue to firmly support each other,\u201d he said.\n\nAmbassador Qi placed the bilateral relationship within the context of China\u2019s broader foreign policy, arguing that the international system was facing increasing geopolitical uncertainty.\n\n\u201cThe global landscape is undergoing profound changes, and hegemonism and power politics continue to prevail. The international community faces the danger of a return to the law of the jungle,\u201d he said."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-07-25-dailyftlk-e16240ef",
    "num": "dailyftlk-e16240ef",
    "date_str": "2026-07-25",
    "description": "China pledges deeper defence ties with Sri Lanka as Beijing marks PLA anniversary",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/opinion/China-pledges-deeper-defence-ties-with-Sri-Lanka-as-Beijing-marks-PLA-anniversary/14-795129",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1784919080.0,
