    "chunk_size_bytes": 1796,
    "chunk_text": "My wife and I have also spent many Sinhala and Tamil New Years, Vesak Festivals, and Poya days participating in a dazzling array of cultural and people-to-people exchange activities in Sri Lanka. Together, our two countries have composed a new chapter of dialogue, mutual learning, closer interaction, and mutual inspiration among civilisations in the new era.\n\nMy wife and I have also visited numerous kovils, mosques, churches, and other places of worship to distribute food packages, maintaining good interactions with believers of all faiths.\n\nThis journey has witnessed mutual trust and support between China and Sri Lanka stand as firm as Sigiriya Lion Rock. China and Sri Lanka have always steadfastly upheld the international system with the UN at its core, the international order underpinned by international law, and the basic norms governing international relations based on the purposes and principles of the UN Charter.\n\nWe have adhered to the Five Principles of Peaceful Coexistence, supported and coordinated with each other in multilateral fields, and safeguarded each other\u2019s core interests and international fairness and justice, sending a strong message of Global South solidarity and self-reliance, as well as a shared commitment to regional peace, stability, development, and prosperity. Our two countries are jointly advancing the building of a community with a shared future for humanity and implementing the Global Development Initiative, the Global Security Initiative, the Global Civilisation Initiative, and the Global Governance Initiative so as to address global challenges and create a brighter future for the world.\n\nThe China-Sri Lanka friendship reflects the shared aspirations of our peoples, and China-Sri Lanka cooperation represents the trend of the times."
  },
